  "Question": "Which of the following expressions can be calculated using the difference of squares formula?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((x+y)(x-y)\\)",
    "B": "\\((x+y)(x+y)\\)",
    "C": "\\((x+y)(-x-y)\\)",
    "D": "\\((x-y)(y-x)\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The difference of squares formula requires one pair of terms to be identical and the other pair to be additive inverses. \\((x+y)(x-y)\\) satisfies this condition; the other three are perfect-square forms (or their negatives).",
